    "event_title": "Comedy Box Summer Series presented by Camden Town Brewery ",
    "event_description": "<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">\n<p>This summer, laughter takes centre stage at Fulham Pier as&nbsp;<strong>Comedy Box returns</strong>&nbsp;for a special series presented by&nbsp;<strong>Camden Town Brewery,</strong>&nbsp;in partnership with our friends at&nbsp;<strong>Nice N' Spiky</strong>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Expect an evening of&nbsp;<strong>standout stand-up, sharp&nbsp;wit&nbsp;and plenty of belly laughs</strong>, all set against the lively atmosphere of Fulham Pier. Featuring a line-up of brilliant comedians, Comedy Box is for anyone looking to switch off, settle in and enjoy a night of great entertainment in great company.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The month's line up includes:</p>\n<p><strong><u>Abandoman</u></strong></p>\n<p>Using his trademark blend of audience interaction and razor-sharp improvisation,&nbsp; Abandoman will take you on a magical journey, transforming the audience&rsquo;s likes, loathes and daydreams into hit songs and captivating tales.&nbsp;Abandoman has previously won Hackney Empire New Act of the Year, Best Comedy Newcomer at the Adelaide Fringe, headlined comedy stages at Glastonbury, Latitude, Reading and Leeds, performed in the house band for Alan Carr's Happy Hour on Channel 4 alongside Craig David, played the part of Dictionary Corner in 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown, as well as supported and toured with pop behemoth Ed Sheeran.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Kyrah Gray</u></strong><br /> Kyrah has appeared on Comedy Central Live and BBC 1Xtra&rsquo;s Comedy Gala, she created and starred in Comedy Central&rsquo;s Dating Horror Stories, alongside building a huge online audience with 20M+ views and performing at the O2 Arena as part of Mo Gilligan&rsquo;s Black British Takeover.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Alana Jackson</u></strong><br /><span>Alana Jackson is a Glasgow-born actor and comedian, winner of the prestigious </span><strong><span>So You Think You&rsquo;re Funny?</span></strong><span> competition in 2024. Since then, she has become a rising star on the UK comedy circuit, performing at major festivals and supporting acts including Kevin Bridges and Michelle De Swarte. Her debut show </span><strong><span>&lsquo;Last Orders&rsquo;</span></strong><span> sold out its entire run in 2025, earning rave reviews.</span><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Michael May</u></strong></p>\n<p>Michael May is one of the UK comedy circuit&rsquo;s most exciting rising stars. A regular MC at venues including the world-famous Comedy Store, his warm, engaging style and unique take on the world have made him a favourite with audiences and corporate clients alike. Definitely one to watch!</p>\n<p>Arrive early and make the most of our&nbsp;<strong>pre-show Happy Hour at Orange Box, with 30% off</strong>&nbsp;wine and Camden Hells beer from 7pm to 8pm.&nbsp;It's&nbsp;the perfect excuse to gather friends, grab a drink and ease into the evening before the first act takes to the stage.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Throughout the night, guests will also have the chance to take part in a special competition with Camden Town Brewery. Complete the phrase on a postcard for the opportunity to win some extra special prizes.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>Expect a buzzing crowd, plenty of laughs and a summer evening worth talking about long after the final punchline.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Gather your friends,&nbsp;book your&nbsp;tickets&nbsp;and join us for a night of comedy by the river.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Over 16's only.</p>\n<p>Artists listed are correct at time of going to press, in the unlikely event that an artist needs to cancel the management reserve the right to amend the line up without notice and no refunds will be due.</p>\n</div>",
    "event_summary": "This summer laughter takes centre stage at Fulham Pier as Comedy Box returns for a special summer series presented by Camden Town Brewery. ",
