    "event_title": "The Recovery Run Club Presented by BON CHARGE",
    "event_description": "<p>This isn&rsquo;t just a run club, but a recovery experience.</p>\n<p>The BON CHARGE Recovery Run Club brings together movement, community, and science-backed recovery in one monthly ritual at Fulham Pier. A 5km loop along the river gets your body moving, but what happens after is where things shift.</p>\n<p>Post-run, you&rsquo;ll step into a guided BON CHARGE Recovery &amp; Recharge session, experiencing red and near-infrared light therapy, the same technology used by elite athletes to support how the body restores, resets, and prepares to go again.</p>\n<p>Each session is hosted by a rotating BON CHARGE expert, offering a fresh perspective on recovery, performance, and modern wellness. We&rsquo;ll finish together with coffee or a juice at the pier - because recovery isn&rsquo;t just physical, it&rsquo;s social too.</p>\n<p>Limited to 25 runners, this is an intimate, community-led experience. And it happens on the last Friday of every month.</p>\n<p><strong>Tickets are&nbsp;&pound;5 inclusive of a guided run, red light therapy recovery session and post event smoothie from Alphabet.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>The Running Order&nbsp;</p>\n<p>12:00 &rarr; Meet at the front doors of Fulham Pier<br />12:15 &rarr; Warm-up and 5km run begins (Thames river loop)<br />13:00 &rarr; BON CHARGE Recovery &amp; Recharge session<br />13:00+&nbsp;&rarr; Coffee and drinks in the Riverside Market, Fulham Pier.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>About BON CHARGE</p>\n<p>BON CHARGE is a science-backed wellness technology company, focused on light, heat and recovery. We know modern life disrupts biology, this is where BON CHARGE Restores it.</p>\n<p>As the Official Recovery and Red Light Therapy Partner of Fulham Football Club &amp; Fulham Pier, BON CHARGE brings elite-level recovery technology into everyday routines. Red and near-infrared light are used to support cellular energy, circulation, and recovery processes, helping the body restore after physical and daily stress.</p>\n<p>This is recovery, redefined.</p>",
