    "event_title": "Global Sounds Presents: Tunisian Roots with Soraya Toukabri Quartet ",
    "event_description": "<p><br /></p>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><strong>This August, the Global Sounds Series continues its journey across cultures and continents with a powerful evening of music featuring the Soraya Toukabri Quartet.</strong></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Between two shores, <strong>Soraya Toukabri</strong> crafts a singular musical language where <strong>contemporary jazz meets Arabic poetry and North African heritage.</strong> Rooted in Arabo-Andalusian traditions and the rhythms of Tunisian Stambeli, her work is also inspired by iconic voices such as Oum Kalthoum and Fairuz, shaping a sound world that is fluid, emotional, and deeply embodied.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">As a French-Tunisian singer, songwriter, and composer, Soraya blends original compositions with reimagined jazz standards and Arabic classics, creating music that is both intimate and expansive.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">On stage, the quartet becomes a space of encounter, where Arabic, French, and English intertwine, where improvisation opens dialogue, and where each piece unfolds like a journey between cultures and memories.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Soraya Toukabri Quartet offers music that breathes, connects, and tells stories across worlds. 🌍✨</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\">Global Sounds Series is a programme curated by Telecoteco Productions in collaboration with Fulham Pier, bringing together world-class artists in a celebration of sound without borders.</div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><br /></div>\n<div class=\"ewa-rteLine\"><strong fontscheme=\"1\"></strong><br /></div>",
    "event_summary": "Soraya Toukabri crafts a singular musical language where contemporary jazz meets Arabic poetry and North African heritage",
